#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:5
#: e72f7541851948f992512050b9713cf7
msgid "QACRO Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:7
#: 8eb354ad86f24057b1844d916e0d0470
msgid "QACRO (for acrobatic) is a quadplane mode for advanced users that provides rate based stabilization like :ref:`Copter ACRO <copter:acro-mode>`.  QACRO mode is best suited for aerobatic flight of a copter tailsitter, but is also available for other quadplane types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:9
#: 68ef70355e8047d599e5b4b8b7ac1e78
msgid "Training mode is not implemented and this mode will behave similarly to a fixed wing plane in MANUAL mode, with no limitations on earth frame roll, pitch and yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:11
#: 8464892462bf4a97b700798a42a2413b
msgid "Aileron and elevator stick scalings are set by parameters :ref:`Q_ACRO_RLL_RATE<Q_ACRO_RLL_RATE>` and :ref:`Q_ACRO_PIT_RATE<Q_ACRO_PIT_RATE>`, respectively, with default of 180 deg/sec. Yaw stick scaling is set by :ref:`Q_ACRO_YAW_RATE<Q_ACRO_YAW_RATE>` with default of 90 deg/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:13
#: b83582c701a346d38919de1e02fb6bf5
msgid "To avoid control surface oscillation, it is necessary to reduce control surface deflections at high airspeeds in VTOL modes.  If the vehicle has no airspeed sensor, this reduction is based on attitude (tilt angle from vertical) and throttle setting, since these are generally correlated with airspeed. If an airspeed sensor is available, the reduction is based on the measured airspeed. There are 2 parameters which control gain scaling: :ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK>` and :ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSCMIN<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMIN>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:16
#: 0dcf8ce71fc042d5be8e6d49cd7dc762
msgid ":ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK>` is a bitmask with two bits: BOOST (bit 0): boost gain at low throttle and ATT THR (bit 1): reduce gain at high throttle/tilt If BOOST is set, parameter ``Q_TAILSIT_THSCMX`` determines whether gain boost (default 2) is applied below hover throttle (used for hovering a conventional 3D plane) If ATT THR is set, attenuation is applied at high throttle and tilt angles (used for \"copter\" tailsitters). :ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSC_MIN<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMIN>` (default 0.4) sets the minimum gain scaling at high throttle/tilt angle when ATT THR is active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:22
#: 7381d60d6c0e4b81845f380a454ccb9e
msgid "Parameter summary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:24
#: 26fa7ce2069b4e419bdde4236abd568f
msgid "If gain boost at low throttle values is desired:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:25
#: 63e19ae94cbc4888ae26e87dd4757aad
msgid "Set bit 0 of :ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK>` (value 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:26
#: 0025174147f043bcb31d9dc9b7f3f814
msgid "Set ``Q_TAILSIT_THSCMX`` to the maximum boost value desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:28
#: 481874776b444b58b462610cbd6c1330
msgid "If attitude/throttle based gain attenuation is desired to reduce oscillation at higher airspeeds in VTOL modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:29
#: 3028a9d7a29f4d618a7744e0062a2f4b
msgid "Set bit 1 of :ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSC_MSK<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK>` (value 2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:30
#: 7763c6c49b5542af9d344786a5a468ee
msgid "Set :ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSC_MIN<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMIN>` to minimum desired scale (greater than zero and less than 1) for gain  attenuation based on attitude and throttle. Reduce this value if oscillation occurs at high airspeeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:32
#: abc9303ae8cb47018fdb6f13c7720a40
msgid "If both gain scaling functions are desired:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:33
#: 2ec878578f884a1b926f5e4a5999ae14
msgid "Set :ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSC_MSK<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK>` to 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:34
#: 5658e74184ad46798ddb15c9921e3a14
msgid "Set ``Q_TAILSIT_THSCMX`` and :ref:`Q_TAILSIT_GSC_MIN<Q_TAILSIT_GSCMIN>` as desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:36
#: 2790352d350345f89ec0721cc0621536
msgid "QACRO flying tips:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:38
#: e04d0d8c4b6d4e65bcb1f991c32fda99
msgid "Transitions from QACRO mode to any other Q-mode are not aided by the autopilot: no throttle boost is automatically applied. This is critical when airspeed (or high throttle) is needed for attitude control, as with non-vectored dual motor tailsitters. The safest way to transition is to make sure you have sufficient airspeed for elevon authority if flying level, or to establish a stable nose-up hover before switching out of QACRO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:41
#: 8f75c295e242453b938d7dfe76de6e62
msgid "Hover Throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:43
#: 288376170b324ddf9ca92b151ffaf526
msgid "Usually, it is desired to hover in any mode, at mid-stick on throttle, so that transitions between modes is easily accomplished without throttle position changes. This can be adjusted using the :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER<Q_M_THST_HOVER>` parameter, or automatically learned in QHOVER or QLOITER modes by enabling :ref:`Q_M_HOVER_LEARN<Q_M_HOVER_LEARN>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qacro-mode.rst:45
#: 1f0b57e3734c48579ea0fcb844c2e193
msgid "If :ref:`Q_THROTTLE_EXPO<Q_THROTTLE_EXPO>` = 0 in QACRO and QSTABILIZE modes , then :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER<Q_M_THST_HOVER>`, whether set manually or learned via :ref:`Q_M_HOVER_LEARN<Q_M_HOVER_LEARN>`, is not applied, and the throttle is determined directly from the RC input."
msgstr ""
